--------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. What this covers
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

This license applies to the source code, build scripts, and documentation in
this repository ("the Software"), EXCLUDING:

  - upstream/ — a git submodule pointing at github.com/socquique/TamaPoke,
    used here under ITS OWN MIT license (see upstream/LICENSE). This license
    grants no rights to and imposes no restriction on that project itself;
    anyone can get it directly from its own repository under its own terms.

  - Any third-party asset (character sprites, the app icon image, etc.) that
    is deliberately NOT included in this repository. See NOTICE.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. Personal Use — permitted without asking
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

You may, free of charge:

  - use, read, and study the Software;
  - modify it for yourself — including personal experiments such as
    reskinning the creatures as a different species or animal, changing
    names, or tweaking gameplay;
  - build it and install the result on devices you personally own or
    administer (your own iPhone, your own Apple Watch, a simulator);
  - fork this repository on GitHub for the same personal purposes above.

None of this requires payment or permission, commercial or not.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. What is NOT permitted without the copyright holder's prior written
   permission
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Regardless of whether money changes hands, you may NOT, without asking first:

  a. publish, distribute, or otherwise make available to anyone other than
     yourself any build, binary, `.ipa`, package, or installable artifact of
     the Software or of any modified or derivative version of it — through
     the App Store, TestFlight, any alternative marketplace, a sideloading
     service, a public download link, a GitHub Release, or any other channel;

  b. do the same with a version where the characters, names, art style, or
     species have been substantially replaced (for example: a version of
     this project re-themed around cats, dogs, or any other creature) —
     such a version is still a derivative of this Software and is covered by
     this restriction exactly as the original is. Reskinning the art is not
     a way around this clause;

  c. present a fork of this repository, or a project built from it, as an
     independent or unrelated product;

  d. remove or alter this license, the NOTICE file, or the attribution
     comments in translated source files.

"Distribute" and "make available" include letting someone else install the
app on their device by any means, even for free, even to a single other
person, even inside a private group. Personal use under Section 2 stops at
your own devices.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. Asking permission
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

If you want to do something in Section 3, ask the copyright holder first.
Permission, if given, will be for the specific thing you asked about — it
does not carry over to a different release, a different reskin, or a
different distribution channel.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. Violations
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The first time you are notified in writing that you have violated this
license, your license continues if you come into full compliance and take
practical steps to correct the violation (for example, taking a distributed
build down) within 32 days of that notice. Otherwise, all rights granted to
you under this license end immediately.

